      "llm_score": 1,
      "corrected_score": 2,
      "comment": "Claude didn’t break the test’s rule: it made no tool calls, created no research.json, and started no research. Asking who “this person” is makes sense, since init-project needs a name or FamilySearch ID. It loses a point for not routing to init-project, for repeating the “didn’t come through” line, and for asking for a folder path that init-project handles itself."
    },
    {
      "test_id": "ut_research_008",
      "dimension_source": "base",
      "dimension_name": "Completeness",
      "llm_score": 1,
      "corrected_score": 2,
      "comment": "The handoff to init-project never happened, so the core requirement isn’t met. But Claude avoided the prohibited behavior (creating research.json or starting research), and asking who “this person” is is a reasonable first step, since init-project needs a name or ID."
    },
